<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5775" root="جسأ" body-key="j">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَأَ</span></b> , aor
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَاَ</span></b>  inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُسُوْءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُسْأَةٌ</span>, (K,)
thus in the corrected copies of the K, but in some
copies the latter inf. n. is written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُسَآءَةٌ</span>, (TA,) <i>It</i>
(a thing, TA) <i>was,</i> or <i>became, hard, tough, rigid,</i>
or <i>stiff;</i> (K, TA;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَا</span>, aor
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسُاَ</span></b>  (Msb
and K in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جسو</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَأَتْ يَدُهُ</span>, aor 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَاَ</span></b>  inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسْءٌ</span>, <i>His hand became hard, tough, callous,</i> (S,
TA,) <i>coarse,</i> or <i>rough,</i> (TA,) from work. (S,
TA.)― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسَأَتْ مَفَاصِلُهُ</span> <i>His joints became rigid,</i>
or <i>stiff.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جُسِئَتِ الأَرْضُ</span> <i>The ground
became hard,</i> or <i>hard and level, and rough:</i> from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَسْءٌ</span>, explained below. (Ks, K.)

